# Hollyland wireless-mic USB-C receiver dongle (3547:0407, model 6108).
# Evidence: inputs/lsusb-v.txt [descriptor], docs/device.md.
#
# Grants non-root access to the usbfs device node so holly-usb (nusb) can
# claim IF0 (the HID control interface) without sudo. IF1/IF2 (UAC audio)
# share the same node — but claiming is per-interface, so this rule does
# not enable claiming them.
#
# 2026-11-05: originally MODE="0660" + TAG+="uaccess" (logind ACL for the
# active seat user). Observed twice live on this system: the rule matched
# and evaluated (mode 0660 applied, TAG got ':uaccess:'), but the device
# node never received the user's ACL entry — for the same builtin that
# was working fine on /dev/snd at the same time (verified: getfacl on
# pcmC2D0c). No udevd-loggable reason found. Replaced with MODE="0666"
# so verification is deterministic; the uaccess route can be revisited
# after a genuine replug of a post-rule-install enumeration.
# Re-examine if this repo ships beyond a single-user machine: 0666 lets
# any local process claim IF0 (control only — audio IFs stay theirs).
#
# Install: sudo cp packaging/99-hollyland.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#          sudo udevadm control --reload
#          sudo udevadm trigger --action=add /sys/bus/usb/devices/<sysfs-node>
#              (or unplug/replug — the trigger just avoids the replug)

SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="3547", ATTR{idProduct}=="0407", MODE="0666"
